# Shadowgate, Entryway -- drums, transcribed from the recording.
#
# 3/4: one line a bar, three beats, / between beats. A beat is four slots (a
# sixteenth each, three of a letter is a triplet) or eight written out (a
# thirty-second each, which is what this file uses so every strike is literal).
#   h hat   s snare   k kick   . rest   xN repeats the line
#
# Read off the original by averaging the four times its 96-row block repeats.
# That matters: a single pass drops the quiet third strike of each triplet --
# levels 1.19 and 1.10 against the loud strikes' 2.7 to 3.5 -- and reading it
# that way gave 151 strikes a statement and no triplets at all in the first
# half. Averaged, it is 184 strikes and the triplets are there from bar one,
# which is what the owner had been saying.
#
# The figure, in the owner's words: sss, two hats / hat, sss / three hats.
# Beat one alternates a triplet with a double, bar by bar.

sss.h.../....sss./h...h...
....h.../h...sss./h.......
sss.h.../....sss./h...h...
....h.../h...sss./h.......
sss.h.../....sss./h...h...
....h.../h...sss./h.......
sss.h.../h...k.../k...k...
k...k.../sss.h.../k.......
sss.h.../sss.h.../sss.h...
sss.h.../sss.h.../sss.h...

# Bars 10-15. The owner's ten bars above stop two thirds of the way through the
# statement, which left the last 8.8 seconds with no drums at all; these six are
# the measured transcription, so the loop closes on the figure the recording
# plays rather than on silence. Beat one alternates a triplet with a double,
# which is the only thing that varies across the original's whole statement.
sss.h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
ss..h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
sss.h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
ss..h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
sss.h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
ss..h.h./h...sss./h.h.h...
